! conclusion: Add predecessor-completion pull as a fourth next-move criterion alongside the three criteria cached in the stack's self-model.

  + context: War Room decision WR-14 (2026-05-17). Operator: Joe. Renamed from draft 1's “operator override.”

  + IF:
    The operator executes a move that diverges from the stack's three-criterion recommendation and the divergence produces an artefact required by the recommended move.

  + HOWEVER:
    Reading the divergence as an override treats the pivot as defection, even when the stack has discovered that its recommended move has an unauthored predecessor.

  + THEN:
    Ingest the operator-executed divergence and any predecessor artefact it produced as a fourth signal class, predecessor-completion pull, when Portfolio Inference is stepped.

  + BECAUSE:
    Completing a prerequisite can be the correct way to advance the recommended move even though it is absent from the existing ranked menu.

    + evidence: The twenty-three-day pivot to npt produced the outward exemplar that M-interim-director names as the predecessor to port inward; bulletin 9 explicitly distinguishes this from overriding the stack's recommendation.
